[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186593267 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d0bd118-d691-553c-ab86-7c351d725ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.054" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3d0bd118-d691-553c-ab86-7c351d725ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.054" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592512} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1a44b81-b97d-515f-9778-c810e6bc33c1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "88775e91-1be2-542a-9c6f-edcf3cb49d80" :question/math-academy-id "q-331489" :question/problem "A fair six-sided die is rolled $6$ times. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, what is the probability of getting a $6$ exactly three times?\n\nRounded to $3$ decimal places, the probability is\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "Let the random variable $X$ be equal to the number of times that a $6$ is rolled. \n\nHere, we have the following information:\n\n- There are $n=6$ rolls.\n\n- The probability of getting a $6$ on any roll of the die is\n\n$$\np=\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nSo, $X$ follows a binomial distribution, where $X∼B(6,\\frac{1}{6}).$ We want to find the probability of $x=3$ successes.\n\nThe number of successes of a binomial random variable has the probability mass function\n\n$$\nP(X=x)=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{x}){p}^{x}(1-p)^{n-x},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of experiments, and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment.\n\nSubstituting the above information into the formula for the probability mass function, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X=3) & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{6}{3}){(\\frac{1}{6})}^{3}{(1-\\frac{1}{6})}^{6-3} \\\\  & =\\frac{6!}{3!(6-3)!}{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{3}{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{3} \\\\  & =20{(\\frac{1}{6})}^{3}{(\\frac{5}{6})}^{3} \\\\  & ≈0.054,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186593274 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13387953-67e5-55db-9603-96b07c7cd7a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592388} {:answer/id #uuid "557a5d01-b686-5762-84c3-cb2c23bd7a93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.85" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592578} {:answer/id #uuid "71b70c1d-b868-5567-a6c4-e1f0b925a099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.91" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592652} {:answer/id #uuid "8773a336-582e-58bc-8d2e-c92de652d5a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592700} {:answer/id #uuid "9e82eeb7-4107-504b-8289-d2d267f7f7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8773a336-582e-58bc-8d2e-c92de652d5a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.74" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592700} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4d62433-669f-5529-85c5-6c6adcc89e8e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593169}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "99b7d013-003d-567d-9a25-4182e399709f" :question/math-academy-id "q-90546" :question/problem "The continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x)$ stated below. Given that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{12},$ compute $\\text{Var}[X].$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{2}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{6}, & 1\\le x<3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the variance using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}],$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}-{x}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{1}+{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{18}|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{45}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the variance is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{71}{45}-{(\\frac{11}{12})}^{2} \\\\  & ≈0.74\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186593300 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "401800d2-7e34-5af0-970f-df2ff6dd8ce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592527} {:answer/id #uuid "aec11c0f-849a-5cc8-ac33-795904ad368d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592802} {:answer/id #uuid "d2b995e9-2582-518d-abe5-0d5699dbaed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{25}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592915} {:answer/id #uuid "e7d97e74-34e0-5bad-98ad-4c61ace9e90d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{100}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592958} {:answer/id #uuid "f46c4e1a-7320-5a87-8a7d-5e257a444e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi }{100}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aec11c0f-849a-5cc8-ac33-795904ad368d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592802} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a899ef9-655e-503c-8b8e-4b58825faaf7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593101}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0ae4f8d-a1f7-53e6-a86f-c52954d33a5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-121689" :question/problem "![](images/4d/4d72a1caa88c1a0753f386c8aab657756497279e5bcd95eaaecaad6f1077c03a.png)\n\nThe height of a conical paper cup is $75\\text{ cm}$ and the radius of the base is $15\\text{ cm}.$ The cup is being filled with water so that the water level, $h$, rises at a rate of  $\\frac{1}{{h}^{2}}\\,\\text{cm/s}.$ At what rate is the volume of water in the cup increasing?" :question/worked-solution "First, let's consider the dimensions of the cup. Let's call $H=75\\,\\text{cm}$ the height of the conical cup, and $R=15\\,\\text{cm}$ its radius at the top. These quantities are fixed and do not change with time.\n\nNow, let's consider the water level. We call $h$ the height of the water and $r$ the radius of the cone formed by the water. Both of these quantities, and the water volume $v,$ change with time. In particular, we know that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}=\\frac{1}{{h}^{2}}\\,\\text{cm}/\\text{s},\n$$\n\nand we want to know $\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nWe need to find a relation between $v$ and the variable for which we know the rate of change, which is $h.$ This is given by the formula for the volume of a cone:\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {r}^{2}h\n$$\n\nBefore we differentiate the equation with respect to time, note that $r$ also appears in the formula. So, we need to simplify the formula by writing $r$ in terms of $h.$\n\nNote that the cones formed by the cup and the water must be similar. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{r}{h} & =\\frac{R}{H} \\\\ \\frac{r}{h} & =\\frac{15}{75} \\\\ r & =\\frac{h}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the volume formula as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\frac{1}{3}\\pi {(\\frac{h}{5})}^{2}h \\\\ v & =\\frac{1}{75}\\pi {h}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow that we have an equation relating $v$ and $h,$ we differentiate with respect to time using the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}v & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{75}\\pi {h}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{25}\\pi {h}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{25}\\pi {h}^{2}(\\frac{1}{{h}^{2}}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{1}{25}\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume of water is increasing at a constant rate of $\\frac{\\pi }{25}\\,\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}\\text{/s}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186593301 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37ae2ac6-8a75-5718-9f1d-5911caf5833d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{1}{2(x+2)}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592496} {:answer/id #uuid "59b3c45d-963f-51a9-9aee-76296a126ab3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|(x+2)^{2}|+\\frac{1}{x}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592592} {:answer/id #uuid "845ea9b3-ad0e-57c3-9625-2d1d10b68768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{7}{2(x+2)}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592698} {:answer/id #uuid "8d59f467-7216-5f5a-a8c1-ac522e9d6a50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\frac{3}{7(x+2)}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592717} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a1d983-027b-5975-874a-d4b2de643f8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "845ea9b3-ad0e-57c3-9625-2d1d10b68768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{7}{2(x+2)}+K" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592698} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3e7be03-e99e-5fc2-b0f9-164b6340ae4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593168}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f4625907-6cd5-5edc-a4ca-fc624ae06a4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-3611" :question/problem "Find the integral of $\\frac{1-3x}{x(x+2)^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we convert the integrand into a sum of partial fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-3x}{x(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{B}{x+2}+\\frac{C}{(x+2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,$ $B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(x+2)^{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n1-3x=A(x+2)^{2}+B(x)(x+2)+C(x).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=0,$ we can eliminate $B$ and $C$ and solve for $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-3(0) & =A(0+2)^{2}+B(0)(0+2)+C(0) \\\\ 1 & =4A \\\\ A & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2,$ we can eliminate $A$ and $B$ and solve for $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-3(-2) & =A(-2+2)^{2}+B(-2)(-2+2)+C(-2) \\\\ 7 & =-2C \\\\ C & =-\\frac{7}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=1$ and substituting the known values of $A$ and $C,$ we can solve for $B:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1-3x & =A(x+2)^{2}+B(x)(x+2)+C(x) \\\\ 1-3(1) & =A(1+2)^{2}+B(1)(1+2)+C(1) \\\\ -2 & =9A+3B+C \\\\ -2 & =9(\\frac{1}{4})+3B+(-\\frac{7}{2}) \\\\ B & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{1-3x}{x(x+2)^{2}}=\\frac{1}{4x}-\\frac{1}{4(x+2)}-\\frac{7}{2(x+2)^{2}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate this expression term by term, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1-3x}{x(x+2)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{4x}-\\frac{1}{4(x+2)}-\\frac{7}{2(x+2)^{2}})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{1}{4}\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{7}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{(x+2)^{2}}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+\\frac{7}{2(x+2)}+K,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K$ is an integral constant."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186593304 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ab6e5a8-3afd-59ec-ab02-3b988b830b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592463} {:answer/id #uuid "b53a641f-4a0c-5f8b-b8b3-e4a3d94cca01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592819} {:answer/id #uuid "ca854eab-bb07-5157-a66a-04eebe4c8b76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592890} {:answer/id #uuid "eaccafe1-80a9-5727-a738-47aeb0860282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592968} {:answer/id #uuid "f1eada11-ec2f-5376-a15a-3278b58f4bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b53a641f-4a0c-5f8b-b8b3-e4a3d94cca01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186592819} :answer-field/id #uuid "19b37d70-aba7-59d0-bec2-ea2fe2d82e8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593035}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fa05d63d-6128-5215-b7df-8cfe25e84f32" :question/math-academy-id "q-170657" :question/problem "Given that $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(\\frac{2}{3}),$ compute $P(X=1).$" :question/worked-solution "If $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function: \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}p, & x=1 \\\\ 1-p, & x=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X∼\\text{Bernoulli}(\\frac{2}{3}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}, & x=1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & x=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP(X=1)=f(1)=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80753d19-a4c9-5827-85a8-900aee3ed385" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sec}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593682} {:answer/id #uuid "8481b40e-2889-5f69-b090-ea6166222aa2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15{sec}^{5}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593694} {:answer/id #uuid "9f2485f3-fddd-5bb2-9777-51115be25b3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}{sec}^{2}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593763} {:answer/id #uuid "f020fcd6-173d-5792-8abe-30bcb379354b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}{sec}^{3}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593943} {:answer/id #uuid "f27d2f97-eb00-561b-b1b7-a8d7347c2d26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593953}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f020fcd6-173d-5792-8abe-30bcb379354b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}{sec}^{3}⁡t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593943} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b01e566-519e-55e1-88fb-f0bcc8666cae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "046815a8-cbc7-5275-a6e8-e70bfe63767c" :question/math-academy-id "q-122881" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations $x=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=-15\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.$ Given that  $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ calculate $\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To compute the second derivative, we can use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(\\frac{dy}{dx})}{(\\frac{dx}{dt})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $\\frac{dy}{dx}=3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,$ and we can calculate $\\frac{dx}{dt}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{dx}{dt}=\\frac{d}{dt}(5\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{dt}(3\\operatorname{tan}⁡t)}{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{sec}^{2}⁡t}{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{sec}^{3}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f43581f-900b-581e-b7aa-c1af7f75b058" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593418} {:answer/id #uuid "2495c036-2b27-500e-8f81-0a17fe66f0a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593467} {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc6153-598d-5fa1-bc9f-a36626f9e7b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593640} {:answer/id #uuid "75b38301-bf78-5f60-8077-dc16df1df4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593646} {:answer/id #uuid "d114cad8-6486-5fd4-b356-2a97a44e6207" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "75b38301-bf78-5f60-8077-dc16df1df4b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593646} :answer-field/id #uuid "3538735c-f453-587b-b4bc-ed9404173cb9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594023}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0aedbde9-cc47-5fcb-8d79-97ecb1021438" :question/math-academy-id "q-29075" :question/problem "![](images/e0/e067c8845d7ce24b7f7e62b49bfcf505c21ae49ce047da27ab1fb3b0d4d17046.png)\n\n$\\operatorname{csc}⁡A=$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $csc$ is the reciprocal of $sin.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }.\n$$\n\nWe have that $m∠A={60}^{∘},$ which is a special angle, and its sine has the value\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡A=\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{csc}⁡A & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡A} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13be2041-38a5-5f52-b1e5-c2dd9f95ffe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593426} {:answer/id #uuid "3b5eea8a-8ecb-5cca-8c74-1a41dbd9d72c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593510} {:answer/id #uuid "c4743ba4-c2ba-5031-a6bb-f992f27204c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{18}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593851} {:answer/id #uuid "dbec9359-c558-5957-8e9c-e9a37478b78f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593901} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3f2b3d-3cdf-5df3-923b-eba617aa2b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593931}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea3f2b3d-3cdf-5df3-923b-eba617aa2b34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{27}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593931} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fa636b3-f5de-5d3e-a215-f00fd104d1e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594020}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0dbc51ee-15ed-52a0-a21b-3201565510a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-145119" :question/problem "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFind $P(X<\\frac{2}{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}).$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that \n\n$$\nP(Y\\in A\\,|\\,X=x)={\\int }_{A}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)\\,\\text{d}y,\n$$\n\nwhere ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ is the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y.$ \n\nUsing the formula for the marginal density function for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y}(y) & ={\\int }_{-\\infty }^{\\infty }f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x+y}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}+xy]}_{x=0}^{x=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2+2y-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2(y+1)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the full expression for ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(y+1)}{3}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow recall that the conditional probability density function of $X$ given $Y=y$ for two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability density function for $X$ and $Y,$ and\n\n- ${f}_{Y}(y)$ is the marginal density function for $Y.$\n\nNow, for $0\\le x\\le 2,0\\le y\\le 1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y) & =\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{x+y}{3})}{(\\frac{2(y+1)}{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{x+y}{2(y+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor other values of $x$ and $y,$ the function $f(x,y)$ equals $0.$ As a result, ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ will be equal to $0$ too.\n\nTherefore, the conditional probability density function is the following:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{2(y+1)}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute our probability:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X<\\frac{2}{3}\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}) & ={\\int }_{0}^{2/3}{f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y=\\frac{1}{2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2/3}\\frac{(x+\\frac{1}{2})}{2(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{\\int }_{0}^{2/3}(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}{[{x}^{2}+x]}_{0}^{2/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{2}{3}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\frac{10}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{27}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49797651-d75d-5b8c-9edb-8de32546def2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593556} {:answer/id #uuid "78412886-0716-5e91-bbab-779c43a45715" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593661} {:answer/id #uuid "90a054a7-5132-5cb9-84c7-749d6119541b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.04" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593725} {:answer/id #uuid "92cdf376-3dbe-5d00-88fc-fa0047956eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593730} {:answer/id #uuid "bf771000-640b-5ba4-87c8-a0030264cb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf771000-640b-5ba4-87c8-a0030264cb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593834} :answer-field/id #uuid "63442e50-d2a4-543e-9976-d1c33887296b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594047}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29a9c010-814a-5d5c-a115-d796744175b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-148350" :question/problem "$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{11}{18},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2582,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2664,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Recall that the correlation coefficient of the random variables $X$ and $Y$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\rho =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]},\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\text{Cov}[X,Y]$ is the covariance, and\n\n- $\\text{SD}[X]$ and $\\text{SD}[Y]$ are the standard deviations of $X$ and $Y.$\n\nFirst, by applying the rule of the lazy statistician, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[XY] & ={∬}_{{R}^{2}}xy\\,f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}xy\\cdot (4{x}^{2}y+\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{x}^{3}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}xy)\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{[{x}^{4}{y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}y]}_{x=0}^{x=1}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({y}^{2}+\\frac{1}{6}y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}+\\frac{1}{12}{y}^{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the covariance and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Cov}[X,Y] & =\\text{E}[XY]-\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y] \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{12}-(\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{11}{18}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{108}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correlation coefficient is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\rho  & =\\frac{\\text{Cov}[X,Y]}{\\text{SD}[X]\\cdot \\text{SD}[Y]} \\\\  & ≈\\frac{(\\frac{1}{108})}{(0.2582)\\cdot (0.2664)} \\\\  & ≈0.13,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186594154 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b72c835-2a5e-54b8-a596-7be0be31d2b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593441} {:answer/id #uuid "1c8f9256-3acb-5c0a-96ec-1872de1fabd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593443} {:answer/id #uuid "20175500-90db-545b-a7f1-b3d3e015c503" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593452} {:answer/id #uuid "71734dfc-a4c9-5340-b1c6-a8ef63bf886b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "n" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593643} {:answer/id #uuid "abe0ff57-d153-5119-9968-a1594cc55d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abe0ff57-d153-5119-9968-a1594cc55d31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593793} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e4d37a4-9084-5882-83af-9b73481a9c74" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594005} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05dd736e-243a-5a30-af2b-8eb5fe6a52d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593385} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce32714-cde1-5033-bb4c-8665fc3f085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593716} {:answer/id #uuid "c97713c9-4ccd-5914-9fa4-3a442622d785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593860}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ce32714-cde1-5033-bb4c-8665fc3f085a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "k\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593716} :answer-field/id #uuid "29b4ca65-355d-5f72-9879-738947842b5d" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594012} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c4efc13-49f8-5ca9-9021-ea011d5fe21b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{3}^{k+2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593671} {:answer/id #uuid "970f1f94-3c26-52a1-a116-87440ca787a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{3}^{k}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593743} {:answer/id #uuid "e1f8479b-9849-5724-8bbc-abcbce550d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{3}^{k+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1f8479b-9849-5724-8bbc-abcbce550d65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{3}^{k+1}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186593913} :answer-field/id #uuid "57dc2467-db9b-5dd7-bc76-1c1802694529" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186594043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03fb98b9-77f2-54d2-91d7-858fdde7acbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ide